# ============================================================================
# FlowConjugateHeat / plane Couette flow with viscous heating  (Hydro2, sharp isothermal walls)
#
# Gas (rho 1, p 1, gamma 1.4, cp 3.5 -> T = 1; mu 1e-2, Pr 0.72 -> k = mu cp/Pr = 4.861e-2) between two
# embedded walls a distance h = 0.1 apart; the lower wall (y < 0) moves at U = 0.6 (Mach 0.51), the upper
# (y > 0.1) is at rest; both are held at T_w = 1.  Periodic in x.  Steady state (constant mu, k; exact for
# the compressible equations because the shear stress and the pressure are uniform):
#   u(y) = U (1 - y/h)
#   T(y) = T_w + mu U^2/(2 k) (y/h)(1 - y/h)        max rise  Pr U^2/(8 cp) = 9.257e-3 at mid-gap
#   wall heat flux (into each wall)  q_w = mu U^2/(2 h) = 1.8e-2  = half the dissipation mu U^2/h
# Checks the viscous dissipation, the gas conduction and the isothermal wall flux together.
# Start-up decays like exp(-pi^2 nu t/h^2) (nu = 1e-2: 1e-6 by t = 1.4).
#
# Run (from bin/): mpirun -np 2 ./hydro2-2d-g++ ../tests/FlowConjugateHeat/input_1D_CouetteHeating plot_file=<dir>/output
# Check:           python3 ../tests/FlowConjugateHeat/reference/couette_heating_check.py <dir> [<dir> ...]
# ============================================================================
plot_file = ./tests/FlowConjugateHeat/output_1D_CouetteHeating
# Check:           python3 ../tests/FlowMovingWall/reference/stokes_check.py <dir>
# ============================================================================
plot_file = ./tests/FlowMovingWall/output_1D_Stokes
